WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
What the $@#% is inflation? We keep&nbsp;
hearing about it, but what actually is it?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.900
Imagine a village that has one market where&nbsp;
people buy all of their stuff, their food,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.080
their clothes. But one day the government&nbsp;
shows up because they're worried about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.860
economy of this village. So they tell the&nbsp;
people that if they want to take out a loan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.940
they're going to make sure that the banks will&nbsp;
not charge them a high interest rate. They want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.200
encourage the people to take out loans and spend&nbsp;
money. Oh, and they also drop off a giant pile of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.220
cash for everyone in the village. And everyone in&nbsp;
the village is like, “Sweet, I'm feeling pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.020
rich.” Villagers now are going to their market and&nbsp;
they're buying way more stuff. Many of them have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.640
been eyeing the fancy electric bike in the market&nbsp;
that before they couldn't justify. But now they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.660
totally can because they have all this new money.&nbsp;
The store owner is like, “Sweet, this is great for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:47.460
business.” But he's running out of bikes. In fact,&nbsp;
he's running out of everything because now all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.420
these people have extra money and they're buying&nbsp;
way more than they used to. The store owners,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:56.220
like, “I can't keep up with all this demand.&nbsp;
I should raise prices.” And that is inflation.

